  "content": {
    "id": "p29-q14-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "14",
    "prompt": "A farmer has a field of total area $1200\\text{ m}^2$.\n\nHe sets up his field with fences at $AC$, $CD$ and $BE$, as shown in the diagram.\n\nThe side $AD$ is beside a river, so no fence is needed there.\n\nThe point $B$ is the midpoint of $AC$, and $CD$ is twice the length of $BE$. Let $AB=x$ and $BE=y$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [
      {
        "id": "p29-q14-diagram",
        "role": "question",
        "format": "tikz",
        "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"geometry\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[{\"name\":\"riverFill\",\"hex\":\"D4E8FF\",\"reason\":\"identifies the river beside the unfenced boundary AD\"}],\"reference\":\"source page 29 p29-q14-diagram\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,line width=0.8pt,every node/.style={font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont,text=black}]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\definecolor{riverFill}{HTML}{D4E8FF}\n\\coordinate (A) at (0,3);\n\\coordinate (B) at (0,1.5);\n\\coordinate (C) at (0,0);\n\\coordinate (D) at (4,0);\n\\coordinate (E) at (2,1.5);\n\\fill[riverFill] (A)--(D)--(4.3,0.4)--(0.3,3.4)--cycle;\n\\draw (A)--(C)--(D);\n\\draw[line width=0.4pt] (A)--(D);\n\\draw (B)--(E);\n\\draw[line width=0.4pt] (0,1.76)--(0.26,1.76)--(0.26,1.5);\n\\draw[line width=0.4pt] (0,0.26)--(0.26,0.26)--(0.26,0);\n\\node[above left] at (A) {$A$};\n\\node[left] at (B) {$B$};\n\\node[below left] at (C) {$C$};\n\\node[below right] at (D) {$D$};\n\\node[above right] at (E) {$E$};\n\\path (A)--(B) node[midway,left] {$x$};\n\\path (B)--(C) node[midway,left] {$x$};\n\\path (B)--(E) node[midway,below] {$y$};\n\\path (C)--(D) node[midway,below] {$2y$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
        "src": null,
        "widthMm": 66,
        "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
        "overlayOf": null,
        "transparent": false,
        "axes": null,
        "spec": {
          "sourcePage": 29,
          "sourceRegion": "Question 14, triangle below parts a–b",
          "description": "Right triangle ACD with B the midpoint of AC and BE parallel to CD. A light blue strip outside AD identifies the river. All supplied vertices, dimensions and right-angle marks are retained.",
          "mathematics": "AB=BC=x, BE=y, CD=2y; AC perpendicular to BE and CD; E lies on AD.",
          "answerVisibility": "All diagram content is supplied and remains visible in the question edition."
        },
        "derived": false,
        "reviewStatus": "needs-review"
      }
    ],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p29-q14-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that the total length of fencing is $L=2x+\\dfrac{1800}{x}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=\\dfrac{600}{x}$, so $L=2x+3y=2x+\\dfrac{1800}{x}$.",
          "worked": "Using the area of $\\triangle ACD$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac12(2y)(2x)&=1200\\\\2xy&=1200\\\\y&=\\frac{600}{x}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe fencing is along $AC$, $CD$ and $BE$:\n$$\\begin{align*}L&=2x+2y+y\\\\L&=2x+3y\\\\L&=2x+3\\left(\\frac{600}{x}\\right)\\\\L&=2x+\\frac{1800}{x},\\qquad x>0.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 57
      },
      {
        "id": "p29-q14-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence find the values of $x$ and $y$ that allow the farmer to use the least possible fencing.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=30\\text{ m}$ and $y=20\\text{ m}$. The least possible fencing is $120\\text{ m}$.",
          "worked": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
